// Category: the Subterm Convergence Warning (`checkSubtermConvergence`,
// Theory/Tools/Wellformedness.hs) and the `[convergent]` equation flag.
//
// The flag lives on the signature, and every `equations:` block overwrites
// it, so the LAST block decides.  Here a plain block comes last and the
// warning stays on for `f(x) = g(x)` (wf_convergent_last_convergent is the
// mirror).  `ff(x, y) = pair(x, y)` shows a pair-headed right-hand side in
// angle form.  The eight corpus theories that use `[convergent]` have a
// single equations block.

theory WfConvergentLastRegular
begin

functions: f/1, g/1, a/0, b/0, ff/2

equations [convergent]: g(y) = a

equations: f(x) = g(x), ff(x, y) = pair(x, y)

rule Test: [ ] --[ ]-> [ ]

end
